 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+\\text{i} & -5 \\\\ 2 & 3+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the homogeneous system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}(-3+\\text{i}){x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+(3+\\text{i}){x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the matrix $A+\\text{i}I$ is singular, the system above must have a non-zero solution. This means that one equation of the system is a multiple of another. As a result, we can drop one of the rows and take one of the variables to be the free variable. For example, from the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{5}(-3+\\text{i}){x}_{1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(-3+\\text{i}){x}_{1}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{1}\\in C.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{1}=5,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{-3+\\text{i}}{5}=-\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{1}{5}\\text{i}.$" 13194139535814 true] [17592186367827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367828 13194139535814 true] [17592186367827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367829 13194139535814 true] [17592186367827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367830 13194139535814 true] [17592186367827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367831 13194139535814 true] [17592186367827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367832 13194139535814 true] [17592186367827 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535814 true] [17592186367827 1041 "selection" 13194139535814 true] [17592186367827 1104 #edb/ref 17592186367832 13194139535814 true] [17592186367827 1110 #uuid "d491997a-9175-5259-809d-b95e13173eb1" 13194139535814 true] [17592186367828 1034 "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{1}{5}\\text{i}" 13194139535814 true] [17592186367828 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535814 true] [17592186367828 1111 #uuid "d9fa9dc7-1985-50e8-ba92-8c4f0c74195a" 13194139535814 true] [17592186367829 1034 "\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{i}"